# GENERATED by mvp/scripts/build-audit.mjs from examples/toys/ - edit the
# toy or the spec, then regenerate; tests/audit.test.ts compares.

::l1 [L1: the syllogism, both premises 0.99]: Both premises at 0.99 and the line at 0.99: the instance follows, Socrates is mortal reads 0.985. The control for the five questions below.

  # l1: the control: the instance is derived, both premises held
  @mortal-l1 [Socrates is mortal]: derived, no authored number
  @human-l1 [Socrates is human] 0.99: the ordinary view
  @humans-l1 [All humans are mortal] 0.99: the universal
  $syllogism-l1 [Universal instantiation] 0.99 @mortal-l1 | @human-l1 AND @humans-l1: basic logic, authored 0.99

::l2 [L2: one premise nearly false]: Socrates is human at 0.01, the universal held at 0.99: the instance is left open, 0.505. A line whose premise fails says nothing about its conclusion, so the instance sits at even odds rather than being denied.

  # l2: Socrates is human at 0.01, the universal held
  @mortal-l2 [Socrates is mortal]: derived, no authored number
  @human-l2 [Socrates is human] 0.01: the reader denies it
  @humans-l2 [All humans are mortal] 0.99: the universal
  $syllogism-l2 [Universal instantiation] 0.99 @mortal-l2 | @human-l2 AND @humans-l2: basic logic, authored 0.99

::l3 [L3: the contrapositive]: The universal doubted at 0.7, reading 0.699. With the contrapositive authored beside the syllogism the instance tracks the universal, 0.697. Bare, the instance reads 0.846: where the universal fails the line is silent, and the instance keeps even odds for that share.

  # l3a: the syllogism with its contrapositive authored, the universal doubted at 0.7
  @mortal-l3a [Socrates is mortal]: derived, no authored number
  @humans-l3a [All humans are mortal] 0.7: the universal, doubted
  $syllogism-neg-l3a [Universal instantiation, negated] 0.99 ~@mortal-l3a | ~@humans-l3a: if the universal fails, so does the instance
  $syllogism-l3a [Universal instantiation] 0.99 @mortal-l3a | @humans-l3a: if the universal holds, so does the instance

  # l3b: the control: the bare syllogism under the same doubted universal
  @mortal-l3b [Socrates is mortal]: derived, no authored number
  @humans-l3b [All humans are mortal] 0.7: the universal, doubted
  $syllogism-l3b [Universal instantiation] 0.99 @mortal-l3b | @humans-l3b: if the universal holds, so does the instance

::l4 [L4: the full truth table]: The syllogism as its full truth table, eight half-lines, one pair per row. With the premise at 0.01 the instance reads 0.505, as under the single line of L2; with both premises at 0.99 it reads 0.980, five thousandths under the single line of L1. The table adds rows the instance cannot see.

  # l4a: eight half-lines, the premise at 0.01
  @mortal-l4a [Socrates is mortal]: derived, no authored number
  @human-l4a [Socrates is human] 0.01: the reader denies it
  @humans-l4a [All humans are mortal] 0.99: the universal
  $cell-tt-l4a [both hold] 0.99/0.01 @mortal-l4a | @human-l4a AND @humans-l4a: the instance follows
  $cell-tf-l4a [human, not universal] 0.5/0.5 @mortal-l4a | @human-l4a AND ~@humans-l4a: nothing follows
  $cell-ft-l4a [not human, universal] 0.5/0.5 @mortal-l4a | ~@human-l4a AND @humans-l4a: nothing follows
  $cell-ff-l4a [neither] 0.5/0.5 @mortal-l4a | ~@human-l4a AND ~@humans-l4a: nothing follows

  # l4b: the control: the same table, both premises 0.99
  @mortal-l4b [Socrates is mortal]: derived, no authored number
  @human-l4b [Socrates is human] 0.99: the ordinary view
  @humans-l4b [All humans are mortal] 0.99: the universal
  $cell-tt-l4b [both hold] 0.99/0.01 @mortal-l4b | @human-l4b AND @humans-l4b: the instance follows
  $cell-tf-l4b [human, not universal] 0.5/0.5 @mortal-l4b | @human-l4b AND ~@humans-l4b: nothing follows
  $cell-ft-l4b [not human, universal] 0.5/0.5 @mortal-l4b | ~@human-l4b AND @humans-l4b: nothing follows
  $cell-ff-l4b [neither] 0.5/0.5 @mortal-l4b | ~@human-l4b AND ~@humans-l4b: nothing follows

::l5 [L5: modus tollens]: Socrates is mortal held at 0.05 with the universal at 0.99 and the premise derived: the premise follows the conclusion down, Socrates is human reads 0.044. Modus tollens, through the backward channel.

  # l5: the conclusion pinned low, the premise derived
  @mortal-l5 [Socrates is mortal] 0.05: the reader is sure he is not
  @human-l5 [Socrates is human]: derived, no authored number
  @humans-l5 [All humans are mortal] 0.99: the universal
  $syllogism-l5 [Universal instantiation] 0.99 @mortal-l5 | @human-l5 AND @humans-l5: basic logic, authored 0.99

::l6 [L6: a chain]: A at 0.400 and each step at 0.99: B reads 0.698 and C 0.846. A step is a leaky noisy-OR, one minus half of one minus the step applied to its premise, so a doubted premise leaves its consequences open rather than pulling them down.

  # l6: A implies B implies C, A at 0.4
  @a-l6 [A] 0.4: the reader lowered it from even odds
  @b-l6 [B]: derived
  @c-l6 [C]: derived
  $ab-l6 [A implies B] 0.99 @b-l6 | @a-l6: the first link
  $bc-l6 [B implies C] 0.99 @c-l6 | @b-l6: the second link
